<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Skilled has Ericsson N.Z. contract.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Skilled has Ericsson N.Z. contract.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Contract labour firm Skilled Engineering Ltd said on Thursday it had been awarded a contract valued at more than A$20 million from the Swedish telecoms group Ericsson to build and manage part of a broadband cable television network in Wellington and Auckland, New Zealand.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement accompanying its 1996/97 first half profit result that Ericsson had signed the head contract with Telecom Corp of New Zealand.</p>
<p>It said the construction involved both underground and aerial cabling and would last for 12 months.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
